{"series": "RANKED · TOP 10", "question": "Should the UK spend more on defence, yes or no?", "country": "", "voice_speed": 0.95, "gap": 0.4, "hook": true, "palette": "colour", "accents": [[1, 33, 105], [200, 16, 46], [255, 255, 255]], "hook_lines": ["TOP 10 MILITARY BUDGETS, RANKED", "Where does the UK land?"], "cover": ["TOP 10", "MILITARY", "BUDGETS"], "region": "WORLD MILITARY SPENDING, 2025", "places": {"TOKYO": {"id": "TOKYO", "name": "Tokyo", "lat": 35.68, "lon": 139.69}, "PARIS": {"id": "PARIS", "name": "Paris", "lat": 48.86, "lon": 2.35}, "RIYADH": {"id": "RIYADH", "name": "Riyadh", "lat": 24.71, "lon": 46.68}, "KYIV": {"id": "KYIV", "name": "Kyiv", "lat": 50.45, "lon": 30.52}, "LONDON": {"id": "LONDON", "name": "London", "lat": 51.51, "lon": -0.13}, "DELHI": {"id": "DELHI", "name": "New Delhi", "lat": 28.61, "lon": 77.21}, "BERLIN": {"id": "BERLIN", "name": "Berlin", "lat": 52.52, "lon": 13.4}, "MOSCOW": {"id": "MOSCOW", "name": "Moscow", "lat": 55.76, "lon": 37.62}}, "lines": [{"text": "These are the world's ten biggest military budgets, ranked by SIPRI, from smallest to biggest.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "SIPRI Fact Sheet April 2026", "scene": {"type": "pin", "place": "TOKYO", "head": "TOP 10 BUDGETS", "notes": ["SIPRI, 2025", "smallest to biggest"], "span": 13}}, {"text": "Number ten, Japan: 62 billion dollars, up almost ten per cent.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "SIPRI 2025: Japan 62.2bn +9.7%", "scene": {"type": "pin", "place": "TOKYO", "head": "#10  Japan", "notes": ["$62.2bn", "+9.7%"], "span": 13}}, {"text": "Nine, France: 68 billion dollars.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "SIPRI 2025: France 68.0bn", "scene": {"type": "pin", "place": "PARIS", "head": "#9  France", "notes": ["$68.0bn"], "span": 13}}, {"text": "Eight, Saudi Arabia: 83 billion, six and a half per cent of its economy.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "SIPRI 2025: Saudi 83.2bn 6.5% GDP", "scene": {"type": "pin", "place": "RIYADH", "head": "#8  Saudi Arabia", "notes": ["$83.2bn", "6.5% of GDP"], "span": 13}}, {"text": "Seven, Ukraine: 84 billion dollars. That is 40 per cent of its entire economy.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "SIPRI 2025: Ukraine 84.1bn 40% GDP +20%", "scene": {"type": "number", "value": "40%", "label": "#7  Ukraine: share of GDP", "detail": "$84.1bn, its highest ever", "flag": "UA"}}, {"text": "Six, the United Kingdom: 89 billion, just short of its 2.5 per cent target.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "SIPRI 2025: UK 89.0bn 2.4% GDP, 'slightly short of the objective of 2.5 per cent'", "scene": {"type": "pin", "place": "LONDON", "head": "#6  United Kingdom", "notes": ["$89.0bn", "2.4% of GDP"], "span": 13}}, {"text": "Five, India: 92 billion, just ahead of Britain.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "SIPRI 2025: India 92.1bn", "scene": {"type": "pin", "place": "DELHI", "head": "#5  India", "notes": ["$92.1bn"], "span": 13}}, {"text": "Four, Germany: 114 billion, up 24 per cent in a single year.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "SIPRI 2025: Germany 114bn +24%", "scene": {"type": "pin", "place": "BERLIN", "head": "#4  Germany", "notes": ["$114bn", "+24% in 2025"], "span": 13}}, {"text": "Germany outspends Britain by 25 billion dollars.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "SIPRI 2025: 114 minus 89", "scene": {"type": "compare", "a": {"n": 89, "value": "$89bn", "label": "UK"}, "b": {"n": 114, "value": "$114bn", "label": "Germany"}}}, {"text": "Three, Russia: 190 billion, seven and a half per cent of its economy.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "SIPRI 2025: Russia 190bn 7.5% GDP", "scene": {"type": "pin", "place": "MOSCOW", "head": "#3  Russia", "notes": ["$190bn", "7.5% of GDP"], "span": 13}}, {"text": "Two, China: 336 billion, its 31st rise in a row.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "SIPRI 2025: China 336bn +7.4%, 31 consecutive years", "scene": {"type": "number", "value": "336", "label": "#2  China, $ billion", "detail": "31 straight years of rises", "flag": "CN"}}, {"text": "And number one, the United States: 954 billion dollars, a third of the world's total.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "SIPRI 2025: US 954bn -7.5%, 33% share", "scene": {"type": "number", "value": "954", "label": "#1  United States, $ billion", "detail": "33% of world spending", "flag": "US"}}, {"text": "In total, Europe spent 864 billion, the most SIPRI has ever recorded.", "src": [0], "context": false, "note": "SIPRI 2025: Europe +14% to 864bn, highest ever recorded by SIPRI", "scene": {"type": "number", "value": "864", "label": "Europe, $ billion", "detail": "+14%, highest SIPRI has recorded", "flag": "GB"}}, {"text": "Should the UK spend more on defence, yes or no?", "src": [], "context": false, "note": "", "scene": {"type": "statement", "lines": ["UK DEFENCE:", "SPEND MORE?", "YES or NO"], "flag": "GB"}}], "sources": [{"n": 0, "outlet": "SIPRI", "title": "Trends in World Military Expenditure, 2025 (Fact Sheet, April 2026)", "url": "https://www.sipri.org/sites/default/files/2026-04/2604_milex_2025.pdf"}], "caption": "Military spending ranked: SIPRI's top 10 defence budgets, from Japan to the United States, with the UK sixth on 89 billion dollars. Germany outspends Britain by 25 billion, and Ukraine spends 40 per cent of its economy. Should the UK spend more on defence, yes or no?", "hashtags": ["sipri", "defencespending", "militarybudget", "uk", "outpost"], "notes_full": ["Evergreen ranking (no fresh story cleared the 18h bar on 3 Oct evening)", "World total 2025: $2,887bn, +2.9%, 11th year of growth (SIPRI)", "Germany also outspent the UK in 2024, so no 'overtakes' claim"]}